34,2,,status,Shizue,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
35,2,1,talk,Shizue,,"The volunteer list is mostly the town history circle, who already guide the monthly walks.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Shion,,"@Shizue, that’s a small pool. I found the lab is down to one person with two hundred pieces waiting.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,May,,"@Shion, that’s a bottleneck. My data says people come back for the people, not the objects.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Misaki,,The bay is capped at four hundred kilos a square metre. The last stonework needed shoring.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Sakura,,I found the transport and mount costs are eating the budget before we even open.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Shizue,,"@Misaki, if the bay is capped, we can’t hang the heavy pieces without extra support.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Shion,,"@Sakura, the paperwork delays are the real killer. Two openings slipped because of late condition reports.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""Sakura""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,May,,"@Shizue, the comment slips say the same thing. They want a guide, not a wall of text.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Misaki,,The maintenance log shows four call-outs in opening hours. The bay was roped off.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Sakura,,"@Shion, if the paperwork slips, the transport costs balloon. I saw that in the invoices.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Shizue,,"So we have one conservator, a capped bay, and a volunteer group that’s already busy.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Shion,,"Exactly. The risk is in the delivery, not the design. I want to know where it breaks.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,May,,The head counts say it breaks when the room is empty. I want a show that moves.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Misaki,,I want a show that doesn’t break the floor. The shoring cost was high.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Sakura,,I want a show that doesn’t break the bank. The joiner’s rate is the quiet killer.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Shizue,,"We need to pick a show that fits the people we have, not the people we wish we had.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Shion,,"Agreed. The data points to a smaller, more controlled exhibition.","{""words"":10,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,May,,A smaller show with more presence. That’s what the visitors asked for.,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Misaki,,A smaller show that the bay can hold. That’s what the structure can take.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Sakura,,A smaller show that the budget can afford. That’s what the invoices say.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
