60,3,1,talk,Shizue,,"Option A feels right. The craftspeople are already in the community, and the volunteers can help guide them.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Shion,,"@Shizue, A is low risk. No heavy loans, no complex rigging. The lab can handle the textiles.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,May,,"@Shion, A is exactly what the comment slips asked for. People want to see the makers, not just the objects.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Misaki,,"@Shion, A is safe for the bay. No overhead rigging, no heavy stonework. The floor can take it.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Sakura,,"@Shion, A is safe for the budget. No transport costs, no joiner’s fees. The invoices will be quiet.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Shizue,,"Option B is tempting, but the conservation bench would be a distraction. The lab is already overwhelmed.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Shion,,"@Shizue, B is a trap. The visible bench would expose the backlog. The paperwork for the finds is already late.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,May,,"@Shion, B is too static. The head counts drop when the room is just cased objects. I want movement.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Misaki,,"@Shion, B is risky. The reconstructions are heavy. The bay might not hold the weight of the site models.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Sakura,,"@Shion, B is expensive. The transport for the finds is already in the invoices. The joiner’s rate will spike.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Shizue,,"Option C is beautiful, but the darkened zones and overhead rigging are a nightmare for the volunteers.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Shion,,"@Shizue, C is a disaster. The maintenance log shows the powered displays fail. The rigging is a liability.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,May,,"@Shion, C is too cold. The comment slips say people want warmth, not darkness. The head counts drop in the dark.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Misaki,,"@Shion, C is dangerous. The overhead rigging is exactly what the structural survey warned about. The bay is capped.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Sakura,,"@Shion, C is a budget black hole. The artist studios charge for installation. The transport costs are unpredictable.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Shizue,,"Option D is too far. The loans from partner collections mean more paperwork, more transport, more risk.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Shion,,"@Shizue, D is the worst. The lender paperwork is the killer. The shipping cut-offs are already slipping.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,May,,"@Shion, D is too distant. The comment slips say people want local stories, not foreign routes. The head counts drop.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,Misaki,,"@Shion, D is too heavy. The ship models are dense. The bay will need shoring again. The floor will groan.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Sakura,,"@Shion, D is too expensive. The transport costs for the loans are the biggest line item. The budget will break.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
